    "narrative": "Today\u2019s lineup for the Austin Waves is anchored by **Jackson Merrill** (73.24) and **Kyle Tucker** (69.85), who present our highest efficiency ceilings. **Jackson Merrill** benefits from a favorable matchup against Roki Sasaki; his high score is bolstered by a significant dynamic platoon edge (+13%) and, critically, the pitcher\u2019s slow delivery, which provides a massive +2% boost toward our scarcity-focused SB strategy. Meanwhile, **Kyle Tucker** remains a staple against Walker Buehler, benefiting from the SP\u2019s high xERA and a solid +10% skill advantage. **Nasim Nunez** (68.25) is another high-leverage start today; while his batting order spot is suboptimal, his ability to exploit the opposing pitcher's slow delivery makes him a priority play to capitalize on our SB-heavy team mandate.\n\nIn the infield, **Josh Jung** (66.07) provides the most reliable production against Corbin. We are also leaning into **Andy Pages** (65.74) at the top of the order; his matchup against Buehler allows him to benefit from the same SP skill inflation as **Kyle Tucker**. While **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (57.70) remains one of our more potent bats, he was benched today in favor of **Coby Mayo** (58.49) and **Nolan Schanuel** (58.56). The optimizer favored **Coby Mayo** due to a specific +8% platoon advantage against Alvarez that outweighed the BvP historical edge we hold with **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, and **Nolan Schanuel** earned the nod for his stability at the top of the lineup.\n\nRisk management remains a primary focus, as we are currently operating under \"Lineup Pending\" assumptions for **Drake Baldwin**, **Nolan Schanuel**, **Jacob Wilson**, **Kyle Tucker**, **Jackson Merrill**, **Andy Pages**, and **Josh Lowe**. If these players are shifted down the order or removed from their projected spots, their scores\u2014particularly for **Drake Baldwin** (54.83)\u2014could drop below our floor requirements. We are closely monitoring **Curtis Mead** (58.36) and **Sam Antonacci** (52.38) on the bench should late-breaking injury news or lineup changes necessitate a pivot, but for now, we are prioritizing players with clear platoon advantages and high-speed profiles to maximize our Roto potential.",
